          "content": "Upper back pain behaves entirely entirely different from the typical lower lumbar ache. While lower back pain is usually caused by heavy hips plunging deeply into ultra-soft foam, upper back pain stems from aggressive surface tension compressing the shoulders inward. As the broad shoulder joints hit a mattress that refuses to compress, they are forced effectively forward or upward. This completely unnatural positioning heavily strains the complex muscular web trapped between your shoulder blades and the base of your neck. To help ease this upper radiating stiffness, look for a mattress with zoned structural support. It cannot be totally flat. It must provide a core designed to yield generously at the exact coordinates of the shoulder area, catching the weight smoothly.",
