      "directAnswer": "A firm mattress supports back and stomach sleeping by resisting hip sinkage; a soft mattress yields at the shoulders and hips for side sleeping. The firm Amerisleep AS2 is designed to help support a more level spine if you sleep on your back, and the plush Amerisleep AS5 cushions the shoulder if you sleep on your side.",
      "answersSI": "How much firmness you need follows from the angles your body makes in your usual position. Stomach sleepers generally do better with firmer resistance, which helps keep the pelvis from pulling the spine out of alignment. On a plush bed, the midsection drops and the lower back arches, which is uncomfortable. Side sleepers have the reverse problem: they need a plush surface that lets the shoulder sink in. On a firm bed, the unyielding surface can push the shoulder inward, which may pull spinal alignment out of position. The Amerisleep AS2 supports back and stomach alignment well, while the AS5 is the better match for side sleepers.",
