          "content": "What sits under a mattress determines how evenly it is held, and whether the setup still satisfies the warranty. A traditional box spring has a flexible internal structure, designed in an era of innerspring beds. Most current foam and hybrid mattresses ask for something else: a solid platform, a rigid foundation, or slats spaced no wider than a stated limit. An adjustable base can fill the support role and also change the angle of the head and foot sections. Of the two products compared here, the Amerisleep Foundation is the fixed option and the Amerisleep Adjustable Bed is the motorized one. Neither suits every mattress automatically. Check compatibility, dimensions, weight limits, and warranty language on the current product pages.",
