          "headingLevel": null,
          "content": "The instinct is usually one of two things: reach for a topper because it costs less, or assume a new mattress is the only serious fix. Neither is automatically correct. The right answer depends on where the problem sits, at the surface (comfort, temperature, firmness) or in the support structure underneath, which is where sagging and broken-down foam or coils show up.",
