      "excerpt": "Down is light and endlessly reshapeable, but it flattens with use; memory foam keeps its shape and contours more precisely, at the cost of running warmer. Sleep position settles most of the question.",
      "directAnswer": "Down pillows are light, easy to reshape, and breathable, but they lose loft with use and need regular fluffing or replacing. Anyone with a down sensitivity may want alternative-down instead. Memory foam pillows keep their shape and loft far longer and contour more precisely to the neck, though they can hold more heat unless the foam is ventilated or gel-infused. Side sleepers tend to want the firmer, steadier support of memory foam; back and combination sleepers often prefer being able to adjust down.",
