          "heading": "Applying This to a Mattress Decision",
          "headingLevel": 2,
          "content": "Match the mattress to your primary sleep position and approximate body weight instead of hunting for one correct firmness rating. Side sleepers tend to do better on a softer, more contouring model such as the Amerisleep AS5, while back and combination sleepers often do better on a medium-firm option like the AS3, which balances lumbar support against some give at the shoulder and hip. There is also a low-tech check worth running during a trial period: lie down and see whether a hand slides comfortably into the gap under your lower back, or whether there is no gap at all. That tells you a good deal about whether the mattress is holding your spine near neutral.",
