          "question": "Why is back sleeping discouraged during pregnancy?",
          "answer": "As pregnancy progresses, lying flat on the back lets the growing uterus press its added weight on the inferior vena cava, a major vein, and that pressure can reduce blood flow. This is general comfort guidance, not medical advice — raise any specific symptoms or concerns with an OB-GYN."
