      "excerpt": "A practical guide to keeping a mattress cool in summer: the bedding swaps, room adjustments, and protector choices that matter most, plus when a cooling mattress cover is worth it.",
      "directAnswer": "Keeping a mattress cooler in summer starts with breathable cotton or bamboo sheets in place of synthetic or jersey fabrics, removing any heavy mattress topper or comforter during the hottest months, and keeping the bedroom itself cool with a fan, AC, or an open window at night. A moisture-wicking mattress protector beats a plastic waterproof one, which traps heat against the surface, and for a chronic overheating problem, a cooling-cover or cooling-gel mattress addresses the issue at its source.",
      "answersSI": "Summer mattress heat is best managed by combining breathable bedding (cotton or bamboo sheets), removing heavy toppers or comforters, cooling the room itself, and choosing a moisture-wicking rather than plastic mattress protector. For sleepers who overheat year after year regardless of these changes, a cooling-cover or cooling-gel mattress treats the underlying cause rather than compensating for it.",
