      "directAnswer": "Temperature-control layering works by starting with a breathable base sheet, adding or removing a lightweight blanket or quilt as a middle layer depending on the season, and topping it with a duvet only during colder months. Natural fibers like cotton, linen, or wool improve moisture-wicking at every layer compared with synthetic materials, and the layering approach itself is the main advantage: it lets you adjust mid-season by adding or removing a layer instead of buying new bedding for every temperature swing.",
