          "headingLevel": null,
          "content": "Swapping out an entire bedding set every time the weather shifts is more work than it needs to be. Layering builds the sleep surface from a few interchangeable pieces instead: a base sheet, a middle layer, and a top layer, each added or removed as conditions change. The right materials at each layer are what separate a setup that genuinely adjusts to temperature from one that just feels heavy or thin regardless of season.",
