          "question": "Is it bad to sleep on my back while pregnant?",
          "answer": "Many OB-GYNs recommend avoiding long stretches of back sleeping later in pregnancy, since it can put pressure on major blood vessels. Short periods on your back are usually nothing to worry about — check with your OB-GYN about your particular case."
