          "headingLevel": 2,
          "content": "The position that helps most depends on which joints are affected. For hip or knee arthritis, side sleeping with a pillow between the knees keeps those joints aligned and cushioned. For shoulder arthritis, sleeping on the unaffected side with a pillow hugged to the chest takes weight off the painful shoulder. For hand or wrist arthritis, keeping the hands elevated slightly on a pillow, rather than tucked under the body or head, may reduce morning stiffness.",
