          "heading": null,
          "headingLevel": null,
          "content": "A sleep routine that actually works has less to do with any single trick and more to do with a handful of consistent elements: timing, wind-down, environment, and a few cutoffs, repeated night after night. The most common reason routines fail isn't a flawed approach. It's giving up before the consistency has had time to pay off.",
