      "directAnswer": "Research associates insufficient sleep with weaker attention and slower reaction time, mood changes, reduced immune function over time, and greater appetite tied to shifts in hunger-related hormones. Sleep science also links chronic sleep deprivation to broader health risks. These are established associations rather than a guarantee of what will happen to any specific person, and this is general information, not a substitute for medical guidance on a diagnosed sleep disorder.",
