          "question": "Does sleep position really make a difference for sleep apnea?",
          "answer": "For some people, yes. Back sleeping can make it more likely for the tongue and soft tissue to fall backward into the airway, while side sleeping avoids that specific mechanism. This varies by individual, and it doesn't replace medical treatment."
