      "excerpt": "Sciatica is a structural nerve issue, not something a mattress creates. This piece covers where it actually originates and how sleep position can ease or aggravate it overnight, alongside proper medical care.",
      "directAnswer": "Sciatica comes from compression or irritation of the sciatic nerve, most often because a herniated disc or spinal stenosis is pressing on nerve roots in the lower spine. It's a structural, medical issue — sleep setup doesn't create it and can't cure it. What sleep position can do is shift how much pressure lands on the nerve overnight: stomach sleeping tends to arch the lower back and can make things worse, while side sleeping with a pillow between the knees tends to hold the spine in a more neutral line. The underlying cause still needs a doctor's diagnosis and treatment.",
