          "heading": null,
          "headingLevel": null,
          "content": "Sleep architecture is the pattern of stages the body cycles through overnight: light sleep, deep sleep, and REM, repeating roughly every 90 minutes. Chronic pain can disrupt that pattern, and the relationship runs both ways — pain interrupts sleep, and disrupted sleep is linked to increased pain sensitivity the next day. Understanding that cycle sets realistic expectations for what changes to sleep setup can and can't do.",
